{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>I would not let the light of my face fall</b> — It is known that laughter removes the light of the face of a ruler, but I would laugh, and because of their great fear they would not believe that I was laughing, and <i>they would not let the light of my face fall</i>."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:56.203653724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}